# GetInterviewed — Full Feature Inventory (ordered by user importance)

Source: cross-checked against frontend/src/pages, backend/app/api/routes,
backend/app/services, and sales/plan.md screenshots. This is the planning
list before writing one doc per feature.

## Tier 1 — Core (the reason someone signs up)

1. **Multi-channel auto-apply** — per-search-URL "Auto apply" toggle (Job
   Alerts) + one-click "Auto Apply" on any job detail page. Runs across
   Naukri, LinkedIn, Instahyre, JSearch.
   Pages: JobDetailPage, AlertsPage, NaukriSearchPage, JSearchSearchPage

2. **AI-tailored resume per job + ATS score** — paste a JD, AI rewrites
   every section (summary, experience, skills) to match it, exports PDF,
   scores it against the JD. 2,200+ generated to date.
   Pages: ResumeMakerPage (Generate Resume tab), ResumesPage
   Backend: resume.py, services/resume/

3. **AI cover letter generator** — same JD-in, tailored Markdown→PDF
   cover letter out, no template needed.
   Pages: ResumeMakerPage (Generate Cover Letter tab)

4. **Unified application tracking dashboard** — every application, every
   status (applied / shortlisted / rejected / recommended / discovered),
   across every connected platform, in one place.
   Pages: DashboardPage, JobsPage, NaukriAppliedPage,
   InstahyreAppliedPage, JSearchAppliedPage

## Tier 2 — High-value differentiators

5. **Universal AI Assistant ("AI Reply")** — floating button on every
   page; drafts a human-sounding reply to any recruiter message on any
   channel in one click.
   Backend: assistant.py, services/assistant/

6. **Auto-referral outreach** — sends referral requests to recruiters/
   hiring managers by email and LinkedIn DM, written in the user's voice,
   at scale (1,000+ sent), with reply tracking and "ask for follow-up".
   Pages: ReferralsPage
   Backend: referrals.py, services/referrals/

7. **Calendar auto-sync** — interview invites are parsed straight out of
   the inbox and land on the calendar automatically, no manual entry.
   Pages: CalendarPage
   Backend: calendar.py

8. **Actions inbox (one-click)** — every recruiter reply, connection
   request, and "apply now" nudge lands in one prioritized list with
   Snooze / Done / Dismiss, plus a "Bulk auto-apply" action.
   Pages: ActionsPage

9. **Multi-channel connectors** — Gmail, Google Calendar, LinkedIn,
   Naukri, Instahyre, JSearch all synced live from one screen; WhatsApp
   and Call show as "coming soon".
   Pages: ConnectorsPage
   Backend: connectors.py

10. **Conversations hub** — recruiter messages from Gmail, LinkedIn, and
    Instahyre normalized into one threaded inbox.
    Pages: GmailConversationsPage, LinkedInMessagesPage,
    InstahyreConversationsPage
    Backend: emails.py

## Tier 3 — Supporting tools

11. **Naukri profile optimizer** — per-section profile score (resume
    headline, key skills, summary, etc.) with an AI "optimized version"
    suggestion for each, one click to push back to naukri.com.
    Pages: NaukriProfilePage

12. **Job board / discovery** — browse, filter, and favorite jobs
    aggregated from every source (company, location, salary, skills,
    channel, status).
    Pages: JobsPage, JobDetailPage

13. **Companies & contacts directory** — every company and POC contact
    seen across all channels, with bulk-fill, email verification, and
    duplicate removal.
    Pages: CompaniesListPage, CompanyDetailPage, ContactsPage
    Backend: contacts_import.py, services/contacts_import/

14. **Job alerts / saved searches** — Naukri URL watchers that
    auto-import new postings and refetch JDs on a schedule, with a
    per-alert auto-apply toggle.
    Pages: AlertsPage, NaukriSearchPage

15. **Hot keywords / market intelligence** — trending skills across
    scanned job postings, plus which keywords recruiters actually
    searched to find the user's profile.
    Pages: HotKeywordsPage

16. **Activity / audit log** — full history of every background
    automation run (task lifecycle, connector syncs, failures) plus a
    notifications feed.
    Pages: ActivityPage
    Backend: activity.py

17. **Settings** — profile, resume attachments, application
    preferences, interview availability windows, proxy config, and
    LLM provider choice (OpenAI / Anthropic).
    Pages: SettingsPage
    Backend: users.py

## Tier 4 — Internal / admin (not customer-facing — operator tooling)

18. **Admin console** — user management, global scheduled-job control
    (pause/resume/run-now), LLM token usage & cost analytics, raw data
    tools. Used to run the platform, not by job seekers.
    Pages: AdminUsersPage, AdminTasksPage, AdminLlmUsagePage,
    AdminDataPage
    Backend: admin.py

---

Next step: one doc per Tier 1–3 feature (18 minus the 4 admin items =
14 customer-facing docs), same folder, using this ranking as the
publish order.
